    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) by placing each piece of logic where it belongs and reusing existing derivations:\n\n1. **`Locality.isKnownRegion(String)`** \u2014 added the single source of truth for \"known region\", backed by a `KNOWN_REGIONS` set derived from the existing `CITY_TO_REGION` values (NSW/VIC/QLD). No duplicated region list.\n\n2. **`OwnerSegment`** (new model class) \u2014 a small, pure classifier mirroring the existing `ContactPreference`/`AgeBand` pattern. `of(membershipLevel, locality)` composes `tier(...)` (PREMIUM at level \u2265 3, else STANDARD) and `area(...)` (METRO when `Locality.isKnownRegion`, else REGIONAL).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` and a `formatOwnerSegment` helper that reuses the existing `membershipLevelEvaluator.levelFor(owner)` and `formatLocality(owner)` (which already handles the `customerCode` region) rather than re-deriving anything.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 documented the read-only `ownerSegment` property so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\nThe `MembershipLevelEvaluator` and `Locality` logic were left untouched \u2014 the new code only composes them.",
